# Multi-line entry with shift+enter (internal/tui/editor/model.go's
# KeyNewLine: {"shift+enter", "alt+enter", "ctrl+j"}). It does not submit;
# EventSubmit only fires on plain "enter" (KeySubmit). Shift+enter is only
# its own key under the kitty keyboard protocol; ctrl+j is covered by
# multiline-ctrl-j.steps, which every terminal can run.
@faux testdata/faux/hello.yaml
@smoke
@size 120x40
@requires kitty-keyboard

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE first line
KEY shift+enter
TYPE second line via shift enter
SHOT multiline-shift-enter
EXPECT /first line/
EXPECT /second line via shift enter/
EXPECT_NOT /Hello from faux/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
